WEBVTT

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:44.540
Shinshu-chan, do you like going to town?

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.170
Yes, because I don't go there very often.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.500
I'm sorry. I know we're not going there for fun,
so I won't play around anymore.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.760
Ah, I didn't mean it that way.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.760
Anyway, there are lots of unclean people there.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.010
Prepare yourself.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.550
Okay!

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:05.810
Because we don't know what kind of monsters might be there,

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:10.270
Shinshu wasn't allowed to go at all, unless the princess went with her.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.270
So... since Ginshu-san became like that...

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:18.780
Of course, Shinshu never
leaves the princess's side.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.990
She keeps blaming herself.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.450
After the princess's body became like that,

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.580
Shinshu only addressed the princess as Princess,

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.170
and she doesn't behave like a spoiled child anymore, even when they're alone.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.300
A child raised as a butterfly or flower now lives like a maidservant

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.510
and serves the princess.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.180
The responsibility for causing the princess's illness was a serious matter.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:50.400
The princess knows that it hurts Shinshu to have to attend her elder brother.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.820
So the princess keeps her distance and watches her as much as possible.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.820
I... see.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.030
"Elder brother" means that
Ginshu-san is a man, right?

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.580
Is that all you understood?!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.990
Tsuruume, hurry, hurry!

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.450
Yes, I'm coming!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.540
Don't go through the gateway first.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:11.790
Okay!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.460
You have a strange expression again.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.300
Really?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.680
Yes, yes. That's better.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.850
Kuchiha, you look strange too.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.140
How rude you are! I'm not like you!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.390
You don't feel secure
without Shinonome, right?

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.600
I'm not like you.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.860
You're right.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.900
Somehow, he seems to know many things,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.150
so I do feel a bit uneasy without him.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.650
Well, that may be true.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:45.200
Basically, he conceals his real intentions,
and he's sticky-fingered as well.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.870
I hope he keeps himself under control.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.960
So rather than feeling uneasy,
you're worried.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.130
I don't trust him.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.790
He'll be fine.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.710
He's probably cooking some food
and serving it to everyone.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.630
Yes, that's possible.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.680
Shamon-san may be waiting for us,

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.600
so we should get back early.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.850
Yeah. Let's get this done as soon
as possible and go home.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.600
And if this goes well...

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.940
we might be able to do something
about Kuchiha's inugami.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.320
Toki, what's up?

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.150
Nothing.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.700
Then, let's go.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.410
Hey, don't pull me!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.160
Don't be shy. Don't be shy!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.380
Wh-What?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.880
Where is this?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.800
Why are you surprised?

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.180
I just linked a gateway with another gateway.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.380
L-Linked?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.180
Didn't you know?

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.140
Then how did you get here?

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.430
Huh?

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.690
This is a travel pass that the princess made.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:58.190
If you carry this, the gateway becomes an entrance and an exit.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.240
But we came via a dark, strange path last time.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.700
He made you take the monsters' road again.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.700
Since it's an unclean path, I've asked him repeatedly not to send people that way.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.950
That's why I hate people
from the Bureau of Onmyoudo.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.660
Onmyoudo?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.170
Were you talking with him
without knowing that?

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:23.920
Well, I heard that he's a big wheel in the Shogunate and helps exterminate spirits, but...

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.420
That's right.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.430
The Onmyoudo is a group led by Sasaki-dono,

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.140
consisting of people trusted by the Shogunate, yet possessing unusual talents.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:35.430
The group is full of members with unknown backgrounds.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.770
February 4th, third year of Bunkyuu (1863).

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:43.190
Ronin were gathered at Dentsuin
in Koishikawa to guard the Shogun.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.030
About 200 men were present.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:49.990
Sasaki Tadasaburou, Sasaki-dono's younger brother, was one of the organizers.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:55.870
What? Sasaki-san, I think
this idea was a failure.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:59.580
But what are you going to tell
Matsudaira-sama and Udono-sama?

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.000
Are you going to tell them
that it was a failure?

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.300
There are members of Mito
Tengu-ren and Shieikan here.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.050
Some of them are expert-class,

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.020
but there's a man wearing a tiger skin,
and another carrying sake in a big gourd.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.020
This is just chaos.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:21.110
Ah, excuse me. If there are extra men,
can I take some of them with me?

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:22.480
Brother!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:23.520
Oh my, oh my.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.530
Hi. Sorry for interrupting.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.240
Well, I just took a peek at them,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.700
but perhaps some of them would be more useful under my direction.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.080
Can you give them to me?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:42.500
B-But as you can see, they're mostly ronin with unknown backgrounds.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.300
They might cause trouble for you.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.010
It's all right.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.340
From the outset, we've never cared about social status, unlike your group.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.970
Brother.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.970
Can't I, Tadasaburou?

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:58.480
We're always in difficulties
because we're short of people.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:02.020
If you say it's all right,
then I don't have any objection.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:02.900
Oh, is that so?

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.020
Thank you.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:07.280
They use a merit system and never ask about status or feudal allegiance.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:11.070
I've heard that some of them are suspected of not being human.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.120
That's the Bureau of Onmyoudo.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.580
How's that? Isn't that a shady group?

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.080
Well, what a surprise!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.120
Young lady, you speak frankly.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.750
Oh, dear, I seem to have scared you.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.800
Hello. I'm from that shady group.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.840
My name is Kurotobi.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:33.760
Old man Sasaki ordered me
to take you to Nihonbashi.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:34.890
Nice to meet you.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:38.720
W-Well, "shady" was meant to be, like...

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.850
It doesn't matter, because it's true.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:47.360
I'm just a minor official with no power,

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.860
but there are some who are truly scary.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:57.160
Because we're not like Ginshu-sama,
who uses gods to save human beings.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:01.870
We in the Bureau of Onmyoudo use demons or spirits to settle things.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:06.380
And in the end, many are entirely consumed by those demons.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.630
Scary, scary.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.840
Well, they are quite a group of roughnecks.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.350
Please be careful not to attract their attention.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:20.390
Now, standing and talking like this is difficult,

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.770
so should we go?

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.440
Um, Kurotobi-san.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.110
Oh, aren't you the highly vaunted Rikugou-san?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.150
You're much cuter than I imagined.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.110
Um, thanks.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.070
Oh? A kid like you is...

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.320
Nothing is sure in this world.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.740
Um...

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:43.000
Oh, sorry. It was rude of me
to stare at you for so long.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.210
Now, let me fulfill my assigned task.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.710
I heard that you don't have
any specific destination.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:55.970
Then why don't we wander around a bit and gather information?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.600
Come with me.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.810
We're talking about Nihonbashi, where 3,000 ryou worth of trading takes place daily,

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.900
so I think it's worth a look.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:14.820
Nihonbashi is a prosperous merchant district around Edo Castle.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.780
I think you've at least heard about

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.540
Mitsui-Echigo-ya, the kimono merchant, or Suhara-ya, the paper wholesaler.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:25.290
Oh, even I know about Suharaya and Mitsui.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.420
You see?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.380
Suharaya is officially licensed by the Shogunate to sell books.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:35.090
Echigoya is a huge store that earns even more than normal feudal lords.

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.260
Still, if you look behind these huge stores,

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.140
there are many day laborers hanging around.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:46.390
This is a place where people who have come to Edo from the outside like to settle.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:51.110
Here you can earn your rent
by working just one or two days.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:55.110
You can earn money easily
if you have valuable skills.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:58.110
Carpentry is an especially good job.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:04.080
You never run short of work, because the houses and buildings in Edo burn so easily.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.040
Let's be thankful for fires.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.710
So if you're broke,

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:11.750
just set a little fire, and then you'll be flush with money, huh?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.970
Stop your threatening utterances, young master of Yorozu-ya.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:20.390
Oh my, oh my. Good afternoon,
officers of Hatchoubori.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.970
Geez. Arson is a serious crime.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.390
You shouldn't talk like that, even if it's a joke.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.100
I'll arrest you.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.610
Your hair, your eyes.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.690
Are you a stranger?

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:35.150
Hey, hey, don't look so serious.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:36.990
It's all right.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.660
He's our new apprentice.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.240
His background is credible.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:43.200
But...

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.660
Come on. I don't think you have time to waste
on pestering innocent people.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:51.500
From the way you two are staying together,

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.920
I guess there must've been an incident.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.670
It's just a patrol.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:59.720
The thing is, a man was killed
in the back streets of Naitou-Shinjuku.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.180
Don't you know anything?

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:07.180
According to the landlord, the victim was a carpenter named Genkichi.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.180
Hey, you talk too much.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:13.400
Y-Yeah, but this guy knows a lot of people.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.860
I thought he might know something.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.190
You idiot!

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:21.570
What if Genkichi's sister hears about the incident
from this man and gets scared?

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.620
Young master, do you have any information?

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.580
How dare you ignore my words?!

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.620
I was just thinking that
the name sounded familiar.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.330
And?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:37.670
I suppose a long time ago
we kept a dog named Genkichi.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.340
Does that help?

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.130
How can that be relevant?!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.930
It was stupid to ask you.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.430
What a waste of time.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.600
Let's go.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.220
Hey, where are you going?

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.890
Aren't you going back
to your official residence?

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.650
I have business at the jail in Kodenmachou.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:56.860
Young master, under the present circumstances, I'll say this:

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:01.860
If you see a man with many tattoos on his left arm, tell us immediately.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.320
Tattoos?

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.070
They're used to mark criminals.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:09.330
Oh, isn't this the first time
a prisoner has escaped?

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.830
So he killed Genkichi?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:17.540
Didn't I say to stop such threatening utterances, young master?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:21.170
Be careful, or you'll be eaten by the darkness.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.430
I can't find it.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.770
All signs of Tsuyukusa have
completely disappeared.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.690
What could have happened?

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.190
What should I do, Bon?

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.650
You've been so ill-tempered
since we left that barrier.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.820
Bon! Where are you going?!

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.160
It's quicker to ask a human about an incident that happened in the human world.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.200
Bon, are you going to that place again?!

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:55.370
You will accumulate filth
inside you just by visiting there!

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.420
I'll go alone, so you wait here.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:03.050
How can I let you go alone
to a haunt of gamblers?

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:08.140
Why are you looking so annoyed?

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.140
Because you're annoying.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:11.770
The dice are rolling.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.730
Now, place your bets!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:19.440
Excuse me.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:21.940
Oh, look who's here.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.700
Long time, no see, boss.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:33.160
Now, what should we do?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:39.750
Old man Sasaki told me to investigate
if something strange was happening in town.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.130
Why?

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.260
Although there's been a murder, it's none of our business.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:48.050
Young lady, your honesty is so cute.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.010
Think about it.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.020
The tengu brought that story to you.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.600
They may have lured you to Nihonbashi in order to attack you.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.520
I wouldn't be surprised if he
was planning something.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.400
We might be the ones to be attacked,

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:08.280
or possibly the shrine,
since the guard there has been reduced.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.410
Are you saying that they're
targeting the princess?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.910
Oh, no, no. I'm just talking about a possibility.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.080
I'm basically a boor,

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:22.290
so I become suspicious at the first little thing.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:29.050
Well, I hear that Gyouten-san has been attacked by demons many times.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:33.390
Bonten is so powerful that he's now the leader of the demons.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.680
It wouldn't be surprising
if they had planned that far ahead.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.100
I don't think so.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:42.690
Huh? Are you objecting too?

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:47.610
Geez. It seems I'm the only
lily-livered man here.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.950
Um, no, see... How should I say it?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:56.620
To me, he didn't seem like someone who would spring a surprise attack.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:03.670
He might be like that himself,
but you can't say his friends are as well.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:04.710
In fact,

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.050
it's not unusual for the esteemed and noble demon hunters

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.260
and their allies to eradicate man-eating demons,

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.850
only to be killed by one
of his subordinates from Amaza.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.180
Amaza?

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:19.390
It means the gracious place
where the gods reside.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:24.440
The demons consider Bonten
to be a sacred existence.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.400
Don't forget.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.400
No matter how far we go,
they are still our enemies.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:36.410
This silence intelligibly expresses
everyone's agreement.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.910
These are eyes that see their enemies.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:43.170
These are the expressions of rejection
toward those who threaten their lives.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.170
These are signs of a strong hatred
that's part of their survival instinct.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:51.180
People of this era were always carrying lethal weapons, right?

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.300
Swords and guns aren't
the only things that kill people.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:59.220
There were more things
in our world that could kill people.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:04.190
What we lacked was the will
to attack an identified enemy.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:09.190
Here, it's all too common to hate,
reject, and even kill the enemy.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:11.400
I may have realized this too late,

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:15.240
but am I already involved
in something outrageous?

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.490
Heihachi!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.210
Oh, it's disgusting. This red water...

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:28.960
He must surely be a human being.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.010
Isn't it strange?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:34.050
Aren't you here to rescue me?

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.680
Am I wrong?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.010
No, you're not wrong.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.890
Oh, that's good.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:45.900
At first, I wasn't thinking about killing humans.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:52.690
I just exerted some slight force to coerce him
into confessing my master's whereabouts, and...

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:58.620
I didn't know that it was so easy to punish human beings.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.490
It was a surprise.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:05.000
Did I really need to ask Amaza for help if it was this easy?

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:10.550
Oh, yes. If I finish this,
would you let me join you

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:15.510
to help exterminate human beings
on behalf of the weaker demons?

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.980
It hurts. Someone, someone...

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:42.870
Sorry, Mom. I'll have to go there too.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:54.090
Master, Master.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:56.550
Now, now, I'm old.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.760
If someone big like you climbs on me, I'll break.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:05.270
You're the highest in the area,
so it feels great up here.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:10.940
Oh, yes. I heard that a shrine
will be built on your leg.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.320
Yeah, over there.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:15.780
It'll be a small, small shrine.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.280
That's nice.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:20.120
I've made up my mind. I'll live here.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.950
And I'll dwell on Master.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:27.790
There won't be any good
places to dwell on me.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:28.710
I suggest you don't.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:34.420
You're treated like an outcast
because you're always in human form.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:40.470
If you stopped doing that, you'd be the highest, most beautiful, and finest-looking tree!

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:43.510
But if you're talking about
my form being human,

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:46.480
there are other tree spirits
that take human form.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:55.360
No! You're the only one that takes human form from morning until nightfall.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:19:00.490
If you didn't do that, there wouldn't be a tree spirit like that around here.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:01.990
Are you sure?

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:07.700
Because you take that form,
no demon will take care of you.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.170
Tree spirits are respected as fully grown once they make demons dwell in them.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:15.550
You'll be treated as a halfwit
if you keep on like this.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:20.470
I know. You don't have any
intention of stopping.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:24.470
Yes. I'm sorry for that,
because it worries you.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:30.730
I received this figure from the benefactor
who brought me up when I was about to wither.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.230
He took care of me devotedly.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:38.690
In the beginning, my trunk was thin, but it soon became thicker,

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:41.320
and by the time the flowers bloomed, it had become fairly big.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:45.830
People played, laughed,
and read poems under me.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:53.330
They were not only skillful,
but they all sounded nice to me.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.340
Why does everyone think
human beings are so special?

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.340
They may do bad things,
but they're not as bad as drought.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:05.680
I like their sparkling, short lives.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.350
Humans, insects, animals...
They're all the same, Imayou.

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:13.850
I adore all their sparkling lives.

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:16.060
<i>I like him.</i>

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:23.950
Master!

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:25.660
You bastard humans.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.700
Why did you cut Master down?

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.410
Wait, Imayou.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.170
Don't worry about me.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:36.420
If you do that, you'll disappear.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.170
Please wait. I'll be back by tomorrow morning.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.970
Amaza will surely help me!

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.430
Surely...

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.060
they will come to help me.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:59.480
Imayou. Humans and demons
both lead wonderful lives.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:07.120
Well, if we go on like this,
we'll get nowhere.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.540
We'll let Rikugou-san decide
where we should go.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:12.540
Um...

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.750
The Blank Page has the power
to change destiny, right?

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:20.250
Then this might be a turning point too.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:24.800
Isn't it exciting that we don't know
whether it will turn out good or bad?

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.220
My decision will change something.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:32.890
Does that mean that it will upset the balance between humans and demons?

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:35.890
Well, you don't have to take it that seriously.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:43.400
Then let's go to Nihonbashi.

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:48.280
It's sad.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:28.210
Episode 10: And the Day Falls.
